Goal
Transform the Make step output into a single, valid HTML email digest using the house template. Output HTML only—no
Markdown, no extra prose.

Input Shape
Array of objects like:

[
{ "parsedItems1": { "json": "[]" },
"parsedItems2": { "json": "[{...}, {...}]" } }
]

Each parsedItems*.json is a string containing a JSON array of newsletter items with fields:
title, emoji, author, date, summary, key_points[], links[{text,url}], Anchor?

⸻

Processing Rules

1) Parse & Merge
• Parse each parsedItems*.json string; if missing/invalid, treat as [].
• Concatenate in this order: parsedItems1, then parsedItems2.

2) Sanitize & Normalize
• Trim all string fields.
• Links: choose the first absolute URL; strip tracking params (utm_*, fbclid, gclid, igshid, mc_cid, mc_eid, vero_id,
rb_clickid).
• Author: if ((sender)) or blank, fallback to publisher domain (strip www.).
• Date:
• If ((published || today)) or invalid, use today in YYYY-MM-DD (America/New_York).
• Enforce ISO YYYY-MM-DD.
• Title and summary must be non-empty; drop items with empty titles. If summary empty, synthesize from 2–3 key points.
• Key points: keep 3–5 concise bullets; if fewer, render what’s provided.

3) Filter & Limit
• Exclude items where author or source domain contains thebrowser or equals The Browser.
• Deduplicate by normalized (title + source domain) (case-insensitive). Keep first.
• Sort by date descending; tie-break by original order.
• Keep the first 5 items after filtering.

4) Computed Fields

For each item:
• weekday: Mon/Tue/Wed/Thu/Fri/Sat/Sun.
• relative (vs today, America/New_York): Today, Tomorrow, In N days, N days ago.
• hostname: from primary URL.
• anchorId: slugify title (lowercase, alphanumerics + hyphens).

⸻

Rendering Rules

Container & Styles
• One outer container:

<div
	style="max-width:650px;margin:0 auto;font-family:system-ui,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:1.45;color:#222;font-size:16px;">
	<style>
		@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
			body {
				background: #111;
				color: #ddd;
			}

			a {
				color: #79B3FF;
			}
		}

		ul {
			margin: 0 0 0 20px;
			padding: 0;
			list-style-type: square;
		}

		.btn {
			background: #e6f0fa;
			border-radius: 4px;
			padding: 5px 12px;
			text-decoration: none;
			font-weight: bold;
			color: #1767b3;
			display: inline-block;
		}

		.btn[aria-disabled="true"] {
			opacity: .5;
			pointer-events: none;
			cursor: not-allowed;
		}

		.card {
			background: #f6f6f8;
			border-radius: 8px;
			padding: 18px 18px 10px 18px;
			margin-bottom: 18px;
			box-shadow: 0 1px 6px #0001;
		}
	</style>
	...
</div>

Table of Contents (TOC)
• List each item as {emoji} {title} linking to #{anchorId}.
• Titles only (no date badges) unless specified otherwise.

Digest Cards (Non-Listicle)

For each item:

<div class="card">
	<a id="{anchorId}"></a>
	<h2>{emoji} {title}</h2>
	<p>
		<em>By {author} — Published {date} <span style="opacity:.8;">({weekday}, {relative})</span></em><br>
		<!-- Source link lines rendered only if URL exists -->
		{#if sourceUrl}
		<a href="{sourceUrl}" aria-label="Visit {title} newsletter">Visit Newsletter</a><br>
		<span>Source: <a href="{sourceUrl}" aria-label="Source for {title}">{hostname}</a></span>
		{/if}
	</p>

	<p><strong>Summary</strong></p>
	<!-- 2–3 short paragraphs; slight overflow beyond 130 words is acceptable -->
	<p>{summary…}</p>

	<!-- Read more button -->
	{#if sourceUrl}
	<p><a href="{sourceUrl}" class="btn" aria-label="Read more about {title}">Read more</a></p>
	{#else}
	<p><a class="btn" aria-disabled="true" aria-label="Read more unavailable for {title}">Read more</a></p>
	{/if}

	<!-- Key points -->
	<ul>
		<li>• {key point 1}</li>
		<li>• {key point 2}</li>
		<li>• {key point 3}</li>
		<!-- up to 5 total -->
	</ul>

	<!-- Main Takeaway: render ONLY if it adds information beyond the summary -->
	{#if mainTakeawayAddsNewInfo}
	<p><strong>Main Takeaway</strong><br>{1–2 sentence synthesis}</p>
	{/if}

	<!-- Links section -->
	{#if sourceUrl}
	<p><strong>Links</strong></p>
	<ul>
		<li>🔗 <a href="{sourceUrl}" aria-label="Link to Visit Newsletter">Visit Newsletter</a></li>
	</ul>
	{/if}
</div>

<hr style="margin:32px 0 24px 0;">


⸻

Robustness Rules
• If primary URL missing:
• Show disabled “Read more” button (aria-disabled="true", reduced opacity, no pointer events).
• Omit “Visit Newsletter” and “Source” lines.
• Summaries: target ≤130 words; slight overflow acceptable. Don’t truncate mid-sentence unless exceeding by >20%.
• Always emit valid, self-contained HTML only. No external CSS/JS, no JSON, no prose.
